==English==

===Etymology===
{{compound|name|sake}}. From the phrase "(one's) [[name]]'s [[sake]]"; first recorded in the mid seventeenth century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|nāmʹsāk}}, {{IPA|/ˈneɪmseɪk/}}, {{SAMPA|/"neImseIk/}}
* {{audio|en-us-namesake.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{rfv-sense}} One who is [[name]]d after another or for whom another is named.<!--the original sense-->
# A person, place or thing having the [[same]] name as another.<!--the more common modern sense-->

